Trigger: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{When a freelancer chooses to upload a CV on their profile page.} \\ \hline

Description: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{Allows a freelancer to upload a CV file in a supported format and associate it with their profile.} \\ \hline

Preconditions: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{
\textbf{PRE-1} The freelancer is authenticated. \newline
\textbf{PRE-2} The selected file is in a supported format and within the allowed size limit.
} \\ \hline

Post-conditions: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{
\textbf{POST-1} The CV file is stored and linked to the freelancer's profile. \newline
\textbf{POST-2} The profile shows the CV as available (UC View CV).
} \\ \hline

Normal Flow: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{
\textbf{A. Upload CV} \newline
1. The Freelancer chooses to upload a CV. \newline
2. The system presents a file selection. \newline
3. The Freelancer selects a CV file. \newline
4. The system validates the file format and size. \newline
5. The system stores the file. \newline
6. The system associates the CV with the freelancer's profile. \newline
7. The system confirms the upload to the Freelancer and reflects the new CV in the profile. The use case ends.
} \\ \hline

Alternative Flows: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{

\textbf{A.1 Cancel Upload} \textit{(branch at step 3)} \newline
1. The Freelancer abandons the file selection. \newline
2. No upload is performed. \newline
3. The use case ends. \newline
\textbf{A.2 Unsupported Format} \textit{(branch at step 4)} \newline
1. The system determines that the selected file type is not supported. \newline
2. The system displays an error message listing the supported formats. \newline
3. Return to step 3 of the main flow. \newline
\textbf{A.3 File Too Large} \textit{(branch at step 4)} \newline
1. The system determines that the file exceeds the allowed size limit. \newline
2. The system displays an error message indicating the size limit. \newline
3. Return to step 3 of the main flow.
} \\ \hline

Exceptions: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{

\textbf{EX-01: System Error While Uploading} \textit{(branch at step 5)} \newline
1. The system cannot store the file due to a processing or connection error. \newline
2. The system displays the message ``Couldn't upload the CV. Please try again later.'' \newline
3. The freelancer remains on the current page without the CV being uploaded. \newline
4. The use case ends.
} \\ \hline

Priority: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{Medium} \\ \hline

Frequency of Use: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{Medium} \\ \hline

Business Rules: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{
BR-CV-01: Only a freelancer can upload a CV to their own profile. \newline
BR-CV-02: The supported CV formats are PDF, DOC, and DOCX. \newline
BR-CV-03: The CV file shall not exceed the allowed size limit. \newline
BR-CV-04: A freelancer can have at most one CV associated with their profile.
} \\ \hline

Other Information: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{Uploading a CV when one already exists replaces it (UC Replace CV).} \\ \hline

Assumptions: & \multicolumn{3}{L{11.1cm}|}{The CV file is valid and belongs to the freelancer.} \\ \hline

\end{longtable}

